# ARBITER ruling — ctl-fleet-tasks (U3) — nQ round 1/3

RULING: BAD TEST
ROUTE: test-maker (correct the suite; re-run)
nQ: 1/3

## Rationale

Independently reproduced the 1-pass/6-fail result, then traced the suite
(bash -x) and verified the implementation directly. Both failure clusters are
artifacts of the test harness, not the code:

1. A1a/A1b/A1c/A2/A3 (phantom rc=1): `capture_dump` is invoked through command
   substitution — `out="$(capture_dump)"` (test/ctl-fleet-tasks.sh:86) — so
   `CAPTURE_DUMP_RC=0` is assigned inside a subshell and never reaches the
   parent. Every caller then reads `rc=${CAPTURE_DUMP_RC:-1}` and fails on the
   rc gate. The trace shows the dump itself exiting 0 and, for the missing-store
   case, correctly omitting the TASKS header — exactly the specified behavior.
   The brief's fact #1 (bash 3.2 `"${extra[@]}"` unbound) is stale: the current
   `run_dump` guards the expansion with `${#extra[@]} -gt 0`, and a direct
   simulation of the no-arg path under host bash 3.2.57 with `set -euo pipefail`
   returns rc=0.

2. A5 (awk range closes on its start line): the extraction
   `/function refreshSlow/,/^function [a-zA-Z]/` terminates immediately because
   awk tests the end pattern against the record that matched the start pattern;
   `slow_body` captures only the signature line. The implementation is correct:
   bin/ctl-fleet:380-381 — `function refreshSlow() {` followed by
   `loadTasksStore();` as its first statement, with store I/O confined there.

No assertion the suite can actually reach indicts the implementation. Fixing
the harness (capture rc without a subshell — e.g. have capture_dump write rc to
a temp file or restructure so the caller runs run_dump directly; extend the awk
range past the start record) is the path that serves craft and keeps the loop
honest: green must mean the spec held, not that the oracle was muted.

## Watch item for round 2 (not ruled on)

Once the suite runs green-path, A2 expects unit line `ORCH fleet-task-cli`
while the fixture's `owner_agent` slug is `ORCH fleet-task` (plan uses unit
`title`). If that surfaces red, it becomes a fresh Q on fixture vs renderer —
deferred per brief.

